# Real thread content, kept out of a public repo by a mechanism rather than a
# comment. `scripts/gold-propose-sonnet.mjs` writes `<draft>.sonnet.jsonl` and
# warns twice in its own source that input and output hold real conversations —
# but a warning does not survive `git add -A`. The gold/replay drafts, DK
# curation sets and knowledge exports all use this extension.
# The kg-bench corpora are synthetic fixtures (see their `fixtureId` field) and
# stay tracked.
#
# ⚠️ This is deliberately broad, and the cost is that a NEW synthetic fixture
# also disappears silently — `git add` will not complain, the file just never
# arrives. If you add one, allow it with its own `!` line below and say in the
# commit why it carries no real content. Silence is the safe default here: a
# missing fixture fails a test, a committed transcript cannot be taken back.
*.jsonl
!scripts/kg-bench/corpus/*.jsonl
!scripts/kg-bench/queries/*.jsonl
